# L §5.5: "LOAD-FORKS if one ask reaches more than 64 combinations (after its with pins), counted at load over
# the axes its cone reaches on the item graph".  Seven axes of two options: 2^7 = 128 combinations.
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2016-03-01
  start 2015-11-01
  end 2016-10-31

axis a1
  p "p"
  q "q"
axis a2
  p "p"
  q "q"
axis a3
  p "p"
  q "q"
axis a4
  p "p"
  q "q"
axis a5
  p "p"
  q "q"
axis a6
  p "p"
  q "q"
axis a7
  p "p"
  q "q"

def n: int
  rule base = 0
  rule r1 beats base = 1 when a1 == p and a2 == p and a3 == p and a4 == p and a5 == p and a6 == p and a7 == p

ask q1: n
=== expect
refused: LOAD-FORKS ...
